AB  - For the state of charge(SOC) estimation under unknown parameters, an adaptive fractional-order center difference Kalman filter(AFCDKF) algorithm in the framework of multi-time scales is proposed in this paper. First, discrete state space equations with memory properties are obtained using fractional-order derivatives, and the influence of the initial state on the SOC estimation is weakened via the fractional-order calculus theory. Then, we design a multi-time scale estimation framework to address the problem of large differences in the rates of change of SOC and model parameters. The unknown parameters are estimated at the macroscale by the extended Kalman filter algorithm, and SOC is estimated at the microscale by the AFCDKF algorithm. Finally, we introduce the multi-innovation theory and forgetting factor into the AFCDKF algorithm to further improve the estimation performance of the algorithm, and the effectiveness of the proposed algorithm in this paper is verified by multiple sets of experiments.
